  <article class="tp-article">

  <div class="tp-answer" id="quick-answer"><p><strong>Quick answer:</strong> the average bicep size is about <strong>13.7&nbsp;inches (34.7&nbsp;cm) for men</strong> and <strong>13.0&nbsp;inches (32.9&nbsp;cm) for women</strong>, measured relaxed (U.S. adults 20+, NHANES 2021&ndash;2023). Flexed, the average man measures about 14.1&nbsp;inches (35.8&nbsp;cm).</p></div>

  <nav class="pg-toc pg-toc--steps" id="page-contents" aria-label="Inside this bicep size guide">
